# Testing Guidelines

## Test Categories

### 1. Unit Tests (`tests/unit/`)
- Test individual functions and classes
- Fast execution (< 1 second each)
- No external dependencies

### 2. Integration Tests (`tests/integration/`)
- Test complete pipelines
- May use external tools (mlir-opt, etc.)
- Test cross-component interactions

### 3. Lit Tests (`tests/lit/`)
- MLIR FileCheck-based tests
- Test dialect parsing, printing, verification
- Test pass transformations

## Test Requirements

1. **Every new kernel operation** must have:
   - Parsing/printing round-trip test
   - Verifier test (valid and invalid inputs)
   - Lowering test to vector dialect
   - Target-specific codegen test

2. **Every new pass** must have:
   - Before/after transformation test
   - Edge case tests
   - Error handling tests

## Test Naming Conventions

```
tests/
├── unit/
│   ├── dialect/
│   │   └── test_kernel_ops.py
│   └── passes/
│       └── test_tiling.py
├── integration/
│   └── test_matmul_pipeline.py
└── lit/
    ├── Dialect/
    │   └── Kernel/
    │       ├── matmul.mlir
    │       └── invalid.mlir
    └── Transforms/
        └── tile-matmul.mlir
```

## Running Tests

```bash
make test          # Run all tests
make test-unit     # Run unit tests only
make test-lit      # Run lit tests only
make test-integration  # Run integration tests
```

## Writing Lit Tests

```mlir
// RUN: aikernel-opt %s --pass-name | FileCheck %s

// CHECK-LABEL: func @test_case
func.func @test_case() {
  // CHECK: expected.output
  %0 = kernel.matmul ...
  return
}
```
